## Competition
- Kaggle **RSNA Knee Abnormality Detection** (code notebook submit, ≤9h, no internet at submit).
- Metric: **macro AUC** over 12 binary labels. Inference: **images + series metadata only**. Reports are train-only.
- Dual finals: max-AUC main + separate efficiency student. **Do not submit** until OOF is far above ~0.72 (public top ~0.94). Do not burn both finals on near-identical models.
- User: Kaggle `girishbose`. Repo: `/Users/girish11/RSNA_Knee_Abnormality_Detection_Model`.
- Compute: Kaggle **T4 x2 only**. `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` (one process). Never `pip install torch`.
- Auth: `~/.kaggle/access_token`. CLI is `.venv/bin/kaggle` (not on default PATH).

## Phase
**Supervision first; architecture search is frozen.** The image model already extracts MRI signal. It is trained to copy noisy keywords (`weak_v1` covers 2449/4407; expert recall ~0.34). Hidden-test ~0.94 is expert-quality.

Reproducible S gates: seed42 **0.742**, 3-seed ensemble **0.745**, historical fold1 **0.732**. The old **0.764** was an unseeded outlier; checkpoint missing; do not use it as a gate.

Keep: frozen DINOv2-B fold0 **0.759** (`main-dinov2b-fold0-weak-v1`) and the seeded S ensemble **0.745**.

